# CODEOWNERS - Mobile Security Toolkit
# This file defines mandatory reviewers for different parts of the codebase
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Global fallback - all changes require review from security team
* @securdevengine/security-team

# Security-critical directories require security team approval
/.github/ @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/devops-team
/scripts/owasp_validation/ @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/owasp-experts
/frida_scripts/ @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/mobile-security

# Core static analysis tools
/scripts/static_analysis/ @securdevengine/static-analysis-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Dynamic analysis and Frida scripts  
/scripts/dynamic_analysis/ @securdevengine/dynamic-analysis-team @securdevengine/mobile-security
/frida_scripts/**/*.js @securdevengine/frida-experts @securdevengine/security-team

# Authentication and crypto analysis
/scripts/authentication/ @securdevengine/crypto-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Utility scripts and environment
/scripts/utils/ @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Configuration files
/config/ @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/config-management
*.json @securdevengine/config-management
*.yml @securdevengine/devops-team
*.yaml @securdevengine/devops-team

# Documentation - requires technical writing and security review
/docs/ @securdevengine/documentation-team @securdevengine/security-team
README.md @securdevengine/documentation-team @securdevengine/project-leads
SETUP.md @securdevengine/documentation-team @securdevengine/devops-team

# OWASP-specific documentation
/docs/*owasp* @securdevengine/owasp-experts @securdevengine/security-team

# Security documentation
/docs/*security* @securdevengine/security-team
/docs/*authentication* @securdevengine/crypto-team @securdevengine/security-team
/docs/*rooting* @securdevengine/mobile-security @securdevengine/security-team

# Wordlists and test data
/wordlists/ @securdevengine/content-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Build and deployment
requirements.txt @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team
setup.sh @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team
Dockerfile @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team
docker-compose.yml @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Security and compliance files
LICENSE @securdevengine/legal-team @securdevengine/project-leads
.gitignore @securdevengine/devops-team
SECURITY.md @securdevengine/security-team
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md @securdevengine/community-team @securdevengine/project-leads

# GitHub-specific files
/.github/workflows/ @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/ @securdevengine/community-team
/.github/pull_request_template.md @securdevengine/process-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Sensitive file patterns that always require security review
**/*secret* @securdevengine/security-team
**/*credential* @securdevengine/security-team  
**/*password* @securdevengine/security-team
**/*key* @securdevengine/security-team
**/*token* @securdevengine/security-team
**/*cert* @securdevengine/security-team

# High-risk file extensions
*.pem @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/crypto-team
*.key @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/crypto-team
*.p12 @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/crypto-team
*.jks @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/crypto-team

# Database and config files that might contain sensitive data
*.db @securdevengine/security-team
*.sqlite @securdevengine/security-team
*.env @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/devops-team
*.conf @securdevengine/security-team @securdevengine/config-management

# Scripts that execute system commands
**/*install* @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team
**/*setup* @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team
**/*deploy* @securdevengine/devops-team @securdevengine/security-team

# Team Definitions (for reference - teams must be created in GitHub)
# @securdevengine/security-team - Primary security reviewers
# @securdevengine/mobile-security - Android/mobile security specialists  
# @securdevengine/frida-experts - Frida and dynamic analysis experts
# @securdevengine/static-analysis-team - Static analysis tool specialists
# @securdevengine/dynamic-analysis-team - Dynamic analysis specialists
# @securdevengine/crypto-team - Cryptography and authentication experts
# @securdevengine/owasp-experts - OWASP Mobile Top 10 specialists
# @securdevengine/devops-team - Infrastructure and deployment
# @securdevengine/documentation-team - Technical writers
# @securdevengine/config-management - Configuration specialists
# @securdevengine/content-team - Content and wordlist maintainers
# @securdevengine/process-team - Process and workflow specialists
# @securdevengine/community-team - Community management
# @securdevengine/project-leads - Project leadership
# @securdevengine/legal-team - Legal and compliance
